Package: cd
Title: How far any BC watershed's climate has shifted from your chosen baseline
Version: 0.6.12
Date: 2026-10-17
Authors@R: c(
    person("Allan", "Irvine", , "al@newgraphenvironment.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-3495-2128",
                       affiliation = "New Graph Environment Ltd.")),
    person("New Graph Environment Ltd.", role = c("cph", "fnd"))
    )
Description: Measures how far the climate of any area in British Columbia
    has moved from a chosen reference period: air temperature,
    precipitation, humidity, soil moisture and snow, by season and year
    since 1950, with trends (Mann-Kendall and Theil-Sen). Reads ERA5-Land
    reanalysis from a public STAC catalog of Cloud-Optimized GeoTIFFs, and
    daily air temperature at points. The baseline, anomaly and trend
    functions take any annual series, such as streamflow. Includes the
    functions that build and publish the catalog. Under active
    development.
